# Oracle rubric — the "__NS__" loop's definition of done

*Passive file. Read explicitly by each work-item's `run-prd-test.sh` when that
runner shells out to an LLM-as-judge. Not auto-loaded, not injected. Edit it to
tune what "done" means for this loop; an oracle-rubric edit should re-run the
planted-event verification (define-loop's `references/verify-the-loop.md`) before
it merges.*

The loop's oracle is **hard, judge-capable, and sentinel-cached**: the dispatcher
runs the work-item's runner and gates on exit 0; on first green it caches a
committed sentinel so a non-deterministic judge isn't re-run every tick. There is
**no "soft" advisory oracle** — advisory signal is the reviewer phase, downstream.

A runner for this loop may mix:
- **deterministic checks** (cheap shell — files, routes, build, grep; run first),
- an **LLM-as-judge** graded against this rubric (runs on the residue),
- **project-native tests**.

Every work-item must keep at least one **hard** check (the baseline `local-checks`
floor counts) so no item can pass on vibes alone.

